// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO5/9/10/18/19/23 (E-ink display SPI bus),
// GPIO12/14 (accelerometer interrupts), GPIO13 (vibration motor),
// GPIO27 (RTC interrupt) - see vendor pins_arduino.h.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO26 tagged "button" - confirmed vendor schematic (MENU button SW1, sqfmi/watchy-hardware v1.0 Watchy.sch).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO25 tagged "button" - confirmed vendor schematic (BACK button SW2, sqfmi/watchy-hardware v1.0 Watchy.sch).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO4 tagged "button" - confirmed vendor schematic (DOWN button SW3, sqfmi/watchy-hardware v1.0 Watchy.sch).
// pfodWeb NOTE: UP button (SW4) left untagged - its GPIO differs by hardware
// revision (GPIO32 on v1.0/v1.5, GPIO35 on v2.0) and this single board.json
// covers all revisions selectable via the Arduino "Revision" menu, so no
// single GPIO can be safely tagged - see notes.txt for human review.
// pfodWeb NOTE: no onboard status/RGB LED confirmed - vendor schematic shows
// LED D5 wired directly to TP4054 charger IC charge-status output (autonomous
// hardware charge indicator, not ESP32 GPIO-driven) - left untagged, see notes.txt.
